ming the W chow. So the answer would be Play W2.\n", "output": "Evaluation: The player should discard W2 to maintain flexibility in forming a potential chow in the W suit. Keeping W7 and W9 allows for the possibility of completing a chow with W8 if drawn, which is critical for achieving the All Chows pattern (2 points). Discarding F4 would risk losing the Seat Wind Pung (2 points) and reduce the chance of forming a pair, which is less immediately beneficial than the chow opportunity.\n\nReason: Discarding W2 preserves the potential to form a W7-W8-W9 chow, contributing to the All Chows pattern (2 points). This complements the existing concealed T7 pung (2 points) and exposed J3 pung (2 points), bringing the total to 6 points. A pair of F4 or another meld could push the score over 8 points, meeting the minimum requirement. Discarding W2 is safer than risking the Seat Wind Pung by discarding F4.\n\nAnswer: Play W2"}
